# --- Secrets and local configuration ---------------------------------------
# .env.example is committed; .env never is.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# --- Runtime output ---------------------------------------------------------
Logs/
# The SQLite database is built from migrations, not from the repository:
# scripts/start.sh and start.bat both run `alembic upgrade head`, so a fresh
# clone gets its schema without one being committed.
#
# It was tracked until a merge proved why that cannot work. Git has no merge
# strategy for a binary file, so any divergence resolves it by picking a side
# and the loser goes silently: a merge of two branches that each carried a
# hundred analysed calls produced an empty 4 KB database, and the only symptom
# was the backend failing to start on "no such table: analysis_runs". Sharing
# an analysed corpus means sharing the file directly, or re-running it.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# --- Node -------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Editors and OS ---------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# --- Assistant session context -----------------------------------------------
# A running log of what's been done in Claude sessions on this repo, kept so a
# fresh session (or a different machine) can pick up context without it being
# re-derived. Personal working notes, not project documentation — never meant
# to be shared or reviewed, so it stays local and untracked.
context-so-far.md
demo-plan.md
wording-plan.md

# Imported corpora. A byproduct of the Corpus import screen: the same calls
# the tracked Samples/ files hold, kept per-upload so an import cannot
# overwrite the corpus a stored analysis was made from.
Samples/imported/

# Database backups taken before a corpus re-run. Covered by *.db above; kept
# as its own rule so the whole directory stays out even if something that is
# not a .db is written into it.
Data/backup/

# --- Local tooling ----------------------------------------------------------
# Neither of these is shared configuration any more.
#
# .github/workflows/ci.yml described a GitHub Actions pipeline, and this repo's
# only remote is Azure DevOps — Actions never runs there, so the file has never
# executed a single check. Note what that means: there is no CI on this
# repository at all, and no azure-pipelines.yml either, so ruff, mypy,
# lint-imports, pytest and the frontend suite run only when somebody runs them.
#
# .claude/ is per-developer editor and agent configuration, including a dev
# server port that is a local choice.
.github/
.claude/

# --- Cloudflare Tunnel ------------------------------------------------------
# The example config is tracked; a filled-in one is not. It names a tunnel UUID
# and the path to a credentials key, and the key itself is a bearer credential
# for the tunnel — anything that lands in this directory stays local.
scripts/cloudflared/config.yml
scripts/cloudflared/*.json
